WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:02.538
- I had to take out student loans

00:00:02.538 --> 00:00:05.089
so that I could be able to go to college.

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:08.642
Thus far, that mission
has cost me $88,000.

00:00:08.642 --> 00:00:11.949
I just think, gosh, couldn't
there have been a better way?

00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:12.846
My name is Marvin Logan

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:16.429
and I have a mountain
of student loan debt.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.576
I'm a first-generation college student.

00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:24.334
I was an all-American track and
field athlete in high school

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.797
and due to those merits I was able to earn

00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:28.870
a track and field scholarship

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.352
and then I got hurt and
that changed everything.

00:00:31.352 --> 00:00:32.918
I had to take out student loans

00:00:32.918 --> 00:00:35.354
to be able to compensate
for the athletic scholarship

00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:36.584
that I had lost.

00:00:36.584 --> 00:00:39.089
By the time that I
graduate with my masters

00:00:39.089 --> 00:00:42.006
I'll be closer to $100,000 in debt.

00:00:42.881 --> 00:00:44.068
I certainly think that it was worth it

00:00:44.068 --> 00:00:48.235
but it was a high price to
pay to have a better life.

00:00:49.884 --> 00:00:51.479
What is most important for me

00:00:51.479 --> 00:00:53.797
is that I can take the
experiences that I've learned

00:00:53.797 --> 00:00:56.627
and teach them to my students.

00:00:56.627 --> 00:01:00.599
I work as a program assistant
for Usher's New Look

00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:02.380
which is a non-profit organization

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.335
all about youth
development and leadership.

00:01:05.335 --> 00:01:07.183
One of the things that I do in my work

00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:11.011
is help students evaluate
and navigate student loans,

00:01:11.011 --> 00:01:13.691
financial aid, figuring out
how to make the best choices

00:01:13.691 --> 00:01:15.071
when going off to college

00:01:15.071 --> 00:01:18.621
so they can continue
to develop as leaders.

00:01:18.621 --> 00:01:20.814
Part of the reason that we've come

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:23.915
to the circumstances we have
in college affordability

00:01:23.915 --> 00:01:27.905
is our lack of representation,
not just as young people,

00:01:27.905 --> 00:01:29.398
but as people in general.

00:01:29.398 --> 00:01:30.689
There are probably not too many things

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:33.079
that are more important in this world

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:34.965
than to stand up and be counted.

00:01:34.965 --> 00:01:36.343
If you truly want to be stronger together,

00:01:36.343 --> 00:01:39.285
if you truly want to
make America great again

00:01:39.285 --> 00:01:41.141
you won't be able to do that

00:01:41.141 --> 00:01:44.478
without a solid and sound
investment in education.

00:01:44.478 --> 00:01:47.561
(lighthearted music)

00:01:50.845 --> 00:01:52.762
(ding)

